Basically, you try to get a monster that wants the Amulet to the
Sanctum by moving to the stairs and letting it follow you. Once there,
it will immediately teleport[1] to the high priest/priestess of Moloch
and fight him/her for the Amulet.
When it collects the Amulet, it will teleport back to you;
this means you won't have to clear the entire Sanctum.

While the Wizard of Yendor wants the Amulet, he isn't strong enough
to kill the high priest; the named demons who want the Amulet, however,
are. As Asmodeus can be found in every game and is no real danger
if you are cold resistant (which you should already be at that point),
most players use him for that purpose.
(In fact, I once used Baalzebub for that; note that he was invisible
and I didn't have "see invisible", so he couldn't stun me.)

[1]: Note that "teleport" might not be the correct word for
     this; it will ignore no-teleport restrictions and has
     been described as "warping", too.

